{"study_accession":"PRJNA384289","secondary_study_accession":"SRP106204","title":"Homo sapiens Raw sequence reads","description":"Although counting of circulating tumour cells (CTC) has attracted a broad interest as potential markers of tumour progression and treatment response, the lack of functional characterisation of these cells had become a bottleneck in taking these observations to the clinic. Our objective was to culture these cells in order to understand them and exploit their therapeutic potential to the full.</p><p>Here, hypothesising that some CTC potentially have cancer stem cell (CSC) phenotype, we generated several CTC lines from the blood of patients with advanced metastatic colorectal cancer (CRC) based on their self-renewal abilities. Multiple standard tests were then employed to characterise these cells.","pubmed":"27456153","geo_series":"","n_samples":9,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN06833338","study_accession":"PRJNA384289","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","sex":"not collected","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2017-05-05","attributes":[["isolate","Colorectal cancer patient 41"],["age","missing"],["biomaterial_provider","Julie Pannequin"],["sex","not collected"],["tissue","Blood"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR5499423","experiment_accession":"SRX2779532","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"RANDOM","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2500","read_count":17433820,"base_count":1763141174,"first_public":"2017-05-05","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 2500 sequencing: Colorectal cancer patient 41 - Circulating tumour cells"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN06833339","study_accession":"PRJNA384289","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","sex":"not collected","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap